        "narrative": "<p>Eugene is a small, clear water lake located in the Boundary Waters Canoe Area Wilderness.  The lake is only accessible via portage trails coming from Steep, Fat, Gun or Little Beartrack Lakes.  There are three primitive campsites maintained by the U.S. Forest Service on the lake.  The fish community is simple with only a few species present.  Northern pike are the primary predator species present in Eugene Lake.  The number of pike captured in nets was typical for Minnesota lakes like Eugene.  The average length was 23.0 inches but 27% exceeded 26 inches in length.  One individual was 32.9 inches long and weighed nine pounds.  Pike caught by angling were smaller than those netted averaging only 17.7 inches in length.Eugene Lake is also home to a relatively abundant population of old, slow growing lake whitefish.  The average whitefish captured was 16.6 inches in length and weighed 2.0 pounds. Other species present in the 2001 survey included average numbers of white sucker and below average numbers of cisco and yellow perch.</p>",
